{
  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "The strongest single-factor improvement in the history is the RNA encoder upgrade from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 (config_019→config_031: 0.639→0.678 acc), suggesting that learned RNA representations are the most impactful design axis. The current best (config_031: scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) has not yet been compared against scgpt, another learned/generative RNA encoder. config_043 is a clean single-variable swap (scvi_n200→scgpt) holding all other settings at their validated best (multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, weighted). This directly tests whether the RNA encoder axis can be pushed further or whether scvi_n200 already captures most of the benefit of learned encodings. Given that the RNA encoder produced the largest observed gain (~4 acc points), resolving whether scgpt offers additional improvement is the highest-information experiment: if scgpt wins, it opens a new optimization direction; if it ties or loses, it confirms scvi_n200 as the ceiling on this axis and redirects budget toward image encoder or aggregation refinements."
}

